Modified on 2026-10-23 for Lyra by Akshay K Rooben Abraham and contributors.

KeywordMatcher.kt is copied from Curbox's utils/KeywordMatcher.kt with the
package declaration changed and provenance added. accessibility_service.xml is
adapted from Curbox's app_blocker_service_config.xml. Curbox's event-driven
application/keyword blocker design is reduced to an AI-only redirect service;
the service, policy, native UI, PIN settings and managed-device controls are Lyra
modifications. gradlew, gradlew.bat, gradle-wrapper.jar and wrapper properties
are retained from the upstream Gradle setup. Gradle wrapper components retain
their Apache-2.0 licensing; see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Version 0.2.0 adds a warm glass UI, randomized local popup messages, an expanded
AI catalog and dismissible YouTube Shorts reminders. ShortsPolicy's visible
player IDs are adapted from Curbox hardcoded/ReelAppConfig.youtubeScript.
Bundled Android icon copies have been recolored orange for this version.

Original M57 work is now AGPL-3.0-only. Curbox-derived portions retain GPLv3;
mixed files carry both applicable terms under the licenses' section 13
combination provisions. See LICENSING.md for the component map. Original
assets and the separate Lyra web application retain their existing terms.
No trademark rights are granted. All upstream attribution is preserved.

Version 0.3.0 renames the Android application to M57, adds a guard for its own
App info page with PIN-authorized temporary access, and includes a PWA setup
guide and installed-PWA selector. The package ID and existing settings remain
compatible with earlier Lyra Blocker builds.

When distributing an APK, also provide its corresponding source, build scripts,
this notice and license, including your modifications, as required by GPLv3.
An unversioned link to upstream Curbox does not substitute for the source of the
modified Lyra APK. The in-app licenses screen includes a copy of the GPL text.

Version 0.4.0 adds a separate administrator navigation shell, a scroll-aware
three-tab dock, full-screen password setup/unlock with verified legacy-PIN
migration, administrator pause schedules and escalating failed-login waits.
The standalone project retains the existing package identity and GPL notices.
Android build and real-device verification are pending; planned category pages
do not imply family filtering or expanded Reels support is implemented.

Version 0.4.0 also adds an accessibility-detail settings guard and optional
manufacturer-specific background setup for Samsung, Xiaomi, Oppo, Vivo, Realme
and OnePlus. BackgroundAccess.kt adapts OEM activity entry points from Curbox's
hardcoded/OemAutostartIntents.kt. Native Android battery-exemption requests are
paired with OEM settings fallbacks and supplementary dontkillmyapp.com guides.
These native flows still require build and device verification.

Version 0.5.0 adds configurable StevenBlack hosts-list downloads, category and
exception controls, atomic cached rules, JobScheduler updates, local UDP DNS
VPN filtering and browser-domain interventions. BrowserDomains.java adapts
Curbox's hardcoded/BrowserUrlBarIds.kt package/resource ID catalog. Contributor
metadata and aggregator MIT terms are in HOSTS-SOURCES.txt and StevenBlack-MIT.txt;
no hosts domain lists are bundled. Original M57 code is AGPL-3.0-only; Curbox-derived portions retain GPLv3
as described in LICENSING.md. Android/network/device acceptance
checks remain outstanding.

